# Phase 18 Push ConsumeMessageService replacement seam — 2026-10-21T17:43:15Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Code revision: `8b1a77ff` (`feat(consumer): expose consume message service parity`)
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
Fixture SHA-256: `2ceab3283085fa8335cd3e7a965c1698e10960ae720c76b148af4cb52a196b4b`.

## Source audit and change

- Added the public Rust `ConsumeMessageService` trait, future alias and nullable
  Push owner getter/setter. Custom services receive direct-consume and normal
  Pull submissions, accepted pool updates, adjustment hooks and shutdown.
- Java 5.5.1 routes POP consumption through its separate private
  `consumeMessagePopService`; Rust retains that split after primary-service
  replacement. Built-in primary `submitPopConsumeRequest` remains unsupported.
- Matched Java `ProcessQueue.removeMessage` for in-flight entries, including
  cached count/bytes, removed-offset tracking and returned next offset.
- Extended the Java accessor fixture to record all nine public
  `ConsumeMessageService` signatures. Updated the Phase 6, 10, 18 and release
  compatibility records.
- Explicit null service assignment no longer falls back to the previous
  built-in service for direct, Pull or pool-update paths. Built-in adjustment
  hooks remain no-ops, matching the pinned Java services.

